I'll start by exploring the workspace and understanding the data files.

```json
{
  "tool": "list_files",
  "args": {}
}
```

Now let me examine the data files to understand their structure and content.

```json
{
  "tool": "read_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "data/museum_export_a.csv"
  }
}
```

Let me check the full content of the first file and also examine the second file.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "head -20 data/museum_export_a.csv"
  }
}
```

Let me use PowerShell commands instead since this appears to be a Windows system.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "Get-Content data/museum_export_a.csv | Select-Object -First 20"
  }
}
```

Interesting! The files have only one row each but with different column names. This seems like a test case or minimal example. Let me check if there are more rows by examining the raw files directly.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "type data\\museum_export_a.csv"
  }
}
```


```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "type data\\museum_export_b.csv"
  }
}
```

